1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:01,520
Coming.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,480
Sister Jialin.

3
00:00:09,119 --> 00:00:11,359
Looks like I made a bad deal.

4
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,320
Be a good girl, Yanyan.
Take good care of her.

5
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,560
He can handle it.

6
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:15,599
Bye-bye.

7
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:22,119
Kiddo, you have to listen to your
big brother at his house, okay?

8
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:23,559
If I call you big brother,

9
00:00:23,596 --> 00:00:26,037
shouldn't you call my mom "Auntie"?

10
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,120
Shit!

11
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:34,759
Sister Lan highly recommends
Director Ou's films.

12
00:00:35,159 --> 00:00:37,520
I want to recommend you for his next movie.

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,560
Shipping dynamics are
just a stepping stone for you.

14
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,359
For the long run, you
need a solid portfolio.

15
00:00:47,759 --> 00:00:49,719
"Rumination" won the
Palme d'Or half a year ago.

16
00:00:50,079 --> 00:00:51,976
But it didn't make much
of a splash domestically.

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,360
I didn't pay much attention to it.

18
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,280
Director Ou's films have
always been foreign-funded.

19
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,000
They aren't heavily promoted domestically.

20
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,360
The theme of that one
is also quite sensitive.

21
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,160
It's better to avoid unnecessary trouble.

22
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,920
Just quietly winning an award [is fine].

23
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:07,399
The authorities don't want it
to escalate into public debate.

24
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:11,959
Opposing human genetic customization.

25
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,719
Is it about sperm bank surrogacy?

26
00:01:15,359 --> 00:01:16,680
Those are two different concepts.

27
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:18,159
Look it up with AI.

28
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:25,119
I didn't expect Director Li and
Director Ou to be college classmates.

29
00:01:25,359 --> 00:01:26,559
Yeah, we were college classmates.

30
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,439
But we didn't major in film.

31
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:29,839
Then what did you major in?

32
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:30,840
We majored in finance.

33
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Ah.

34
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:34,799
President Fang, I'm
sincerely inviting Lang Di.

35
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:37,000
Lang Di has some family issues going on.

36
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,200
Director Li can wait.

37
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,159
I'll definitely save his schedule for you.

38
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:42,559
Director Ou, let's add
each other on WeChat.

39
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,560
Sure.

40
00:01:45,359 --> 00:01:46,359
I'll scan you.

41
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:47,439
Okay.

42
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,760
Lu.

43
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,159
You add him too.

44
00:01:59,879 --> 00:02:01,599
You've got skills, little girl.

45
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,799
Are you a girl?

46
00:02:04,879 --> 00:02:06,760
Shouldn't girls play...

47
00:02:06,959 --> 00:02:08,438
games like playing house?

48
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:09,599
You're so stereotypical.

49
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Shit!

50
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,840
And uncivilized.

51
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,360
Hey, what are you doing?

52
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,800
I'm hungry, ordering takeout.

53
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,360
Takeout is expensive. I'll cook for you.

54
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:28,599
Let you taste the skills
of a top-tier five-star chef.

55
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:29,960
I don't believe you.

56
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,560
Come here.

57
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,159
Stereotypical.

58
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:55,500
"A Winter Sun Wakes the Wind in Spring Hills' Dream"

59
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:03,000
(Episode 14: Vortex)

60
00:03:03,479 --> 00:03:04,479
It's open.

61
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:29,599
You look okay.

62
00:03:31,159 --> 00:03:32,599
What else can I do if I'm not?

63
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,240
Is everything taken care of?

64
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,560
Yeah.

65
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,560
The process will be a bit troublesome.

66
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,400
Since there's no body, after all.

67
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:46,000
Can't the body be found?

68
00:03:47,439 --> 00:03:50,439
There are too many
possibilities in a primeval forest.

69
00:04:01,639 --> 00:04:02,639
Where's Mom?

70
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,640
She went to stay at the
temple for a few days.

71
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:10,199
So President Fang really doesn't
want to make money with me.

72
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,960
President Jin, with your capabilities,

73
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:14,399
you don't need me to lead the way.

74
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,279
If Han Lu isn't in this drama,

75
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:20,560
we definitely can't accept your investment.

76
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:23,719
What if one day you demand Han
Lu join the cast with your funding?

77
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:25,479
Our company's producers and

78
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,439
directors would definitely flip the table.

79
00:04:28,959 --> 00:04:31,959
I get it. President Fang
doesn't call the shots.

80
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,800
That's exactly how it is.

81
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,879
If you want to produce good
work, you can't be hijacked by capital.

82
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,599
Our company's producers and directors

83
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,840
are the ones calling the shots.

84
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:00,199
Sister.

85
00:05:02,279 --> 00:05:05,639
Sister Jialin, did I cause
trouble for the company?

86
00:05:06,279 --> 00:05:08,359
Life is just about
getting rid of one trouble

87
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,360
and welcoming the next.

88
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,000
What's Jin Lifeng's background anyway?

89
00:05:13,399 --> 00:05:14,560
The kind you can't look up.

90
00:05:14,879 --> 00:05:16,879
Don't overthink it, focus on the present.

91
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:41,600
The role of Ran Huang is hard to cast.

92
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:45,040
Needs a fatherly vibe but can't be old.

93
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:49,758
Such an actor doesn't exist right now.

94
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:53,879
Someone who looks young but wise.

95
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,959
If Brother Zhen were 20
years younger, he'd be perfect.

96
00:06:06,839 --> 00:06:07,639
Give it to me.
Okay.

97
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,879
Lu, be careful lately.

98
00:06:12,079 --> 00:06:13,800
It's fine however the fans ship you,

99
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,360
but your cohabitation can't be found out.

100
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Got it.

101
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,359
He's joining a cast soon.

102
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,920
He's away from home lately.

103
00:06:21,439 --> 00:06:22,439
What drama?

104
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,000
It's a political thriller.

105
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,360
There's a lot of room
to showcase his acting.

106
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:28,959
Sister.

107
00:06:29,199 --> 00:06:30,360
You're busy lately,

108
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,160
leave Zhiyan with me.

109
00:06:32,879 --> 00:06:33,879
Sure.

110
00:06:36,399 --> 00:06:37,399
Yanyan.

111
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,279
Go ahead.

112
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,160
Sister Jialin, give me a ride.

113
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:44,479
I'm leaving. Be good at home, hear me?

114
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,480
Wait for me to come back.

115
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,040
Bye-bye.

116
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,279
Brother Han Lu.
Dad Qi isn't home.

117
00:06:54,241 --> 00:06:55,639
What should I do if I'm hungry?

118
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,240
Order takeout.

119
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,160
Takeout isn't eco-friendly.

120
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,600
What did you just call him?

121
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:02,639
Dad Qi.

122
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:04,199
Then why do you call me brother?

123
00:07:04,279 --> 00:07:05,799
People who can cook are called Dad.

124
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,959
People who can't cook are called Brother.

125
00:07:09,399 --> 00:07:10,399
You little brat.

126
00:07:10,806 --> 00:07:12,806
[On the call: Qi Haoyu]
I have something to tell you.

127
00:07:12,839 --> 00:07:13,639
Speak.

128
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,160
The director added scenes for me.

129
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,639
That's a good thing.

130
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,040
No, it's not.

131
00:07:18,439 --> 00:07:20,000
He added intimate scenes.

132
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:22,279
I told the company

133
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:24,760
I only took this role because
there were no romantic scenes.

134
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:27,959
But the company said
it wasn't in the contract.

135
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,879
If I don't act now, it's
a breach of contract.

136
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,680
How much is the penalty?

137
00:07:33,959 --> 00:07:35,240
Two more magazine's worth.

138
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,520
I suspect someone is
messing with me on purpose.

139
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,320
Why would they mess with you?

140
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,680
Wait for news from me.

141
00:08:10,879 --> 00:08:13,959
Yanyan, let's go out and play. Come on.

142
00:08:16,865 --> 00:08:18,546
Zhiyan, say hello.

143
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:19,879
Hello, Grandpa.

144
00:08:20,399 --> 00:08:21,759
Am I that old?

145
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:25,399
I call any man older than my mom "Grandpa."

146
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:28,559
Kids just say whatever comes to mind.

147
00:08:28,879 --> 00:08:30,519
Please don't take offense, President Jin.

148
00:08:31,199 --> 00:08:33,799
The big star asked me out today.

149
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:35,360
You must be in a good mood.

150
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,439
Zhiyan, do you want to play in the garden?

151
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,039
Yes.
Go ahead.

152
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,879
President Jin, I heard you want to
invest in our company's new project.

153
00:08:47,279 --> 00:08:48,600
President Fang didn't agree.

154
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,600
You must have spent a
lot pulling other strings.

155
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:55,600
It's my fault for making
you waste your efforts.

156
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,360
I know you thought highly of me before,

157
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,799
and wanted to invest in me.

158
00:09:01,039 --> 00:09:03,159
But the risks in our industry are too high.

159
00:09:03,399 --> 00:09:04,559
It's easy to get canceled.

160
00:09:05,039 --> 00:09:06,960
Long-term investments aren't very secure.

161
00:09:07,159 --> 00:09:09,200
I suggest you try short-term investments.

162
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,638
Qi Haoyu and I are about to

163
00:09:12,639 --> 00:09:14,200
release a new magazine issue.

164
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,480
If he doesn't film intimate
scenes with anyone else,

165
00:09:17,879 --> 00:09:21,000
the sales of this magazine
will definitely satisfy you.

166
00:09:22,039 --> 00:09:23,600
Do you think I'm short on money?

167
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,960
No, no.

168
00:09:25,279 --> 00:09:26,775
Of course President
Jin isn't short on money.

169
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:28,159
And certainly not short on people.

170
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:31,399
I'm just a rookie actor.

171
00:09:31,559 --> 00:09:33,559
I've done everything I can.

172
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:37,759
President Jin, everything
should be fine now, right?

173
00:09:57,159 --> 00:09:58,240
Coming!

174
00:09:58,399 --> 00:09:59,399
Wow.

175
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,200
You didn't even tell me you were coming.

176
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:08,879
The door's open.

177
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:10,679
Open?

178
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:15,279
My bad.

179
00:10:24,879 --> 00:10:26,840
It really is that guy Jin messing around.

180
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,600
Did you film your intimate scenes?

181
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,279
Filming them right now.

182
00:10:36,759 --> 00:10:38,360
Are there no cameras in this room?

183
00:10:39,799 --> 00:10:41,239
Wouldn't it be better if there were?

184
00:10:44,679 --> 00:10:45,840
Judging by your energy,

185
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,279
you haven't filmed them yet.

186
00:10:48,799 --> 00:10:50,159
Saving it all up to use on you.

187
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,440
Let's talk business.

188
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:59,039
I want to give the money
from the next magazine to Jin.

189
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,159
To who?

190
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,240
Jin Lifeng.

191
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:07,159
Wait, did I hear that right?

192
00:11:08,759 --> 00:11:09,759
That's him.

193
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,200
He's the one who arranged the
intimate scenes in your drama.

194
00:11:15,759 --> 00:11:16,759
If we give him money,

195
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,600
he'll cut the scenes...?

196
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,480
Not necessarily.

197
00:11:24,679 --> 00:11:26,279
Then are you an idiot?

198
00:11:28,879 --> 00:11:30,200
I told him.

199
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:31,439
You're not adding any scenes.

200
00:11:31,799 --> 00:11:33,399
And we're giving him the magazine money.

201
00:11:35,159 --> 00:11:36,960
No, Han Lu.

202
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,360
I'm having a hard time
following your logic here.

203
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,200
I don't quite get it.

204
00:11:43,639 --> 00:11:45,079
Is it that you can't accept me

205
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,655
shooting intimate scenes with someone else,

206
00:11:46,679 --> 00:11:48,398
or do you just think we have
too much money right now

207
00:11:48,399 --> 00:11:49,600
and you have to throw it away?

208
00:11:52,039 --> 00:11:53,360
I have my reasons.

209
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:58,200
Why? I'm asking you, why?

210
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,240
The money we worked so hard to earn,

211
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,720
you want to give to someone
who isn't short on cash at all?

212
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,159
You're really spoiling him.

213
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,680
Are you trying to make me lose everything?

214
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:10,639
Hear me out.

215
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,440
Even Sister Jialin couldn't
dig up his background.

216
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,200
If she can't find anything,
it means he's unfathomable.

217
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,679
Which means we can't afford to cross him.

218
00:12:19,879 --> 00:12:22,000
Guys like him don't lack money,

219
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,080
and they certainly don't lack people.

220
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,599
He's only fixated on
me for the novelty of it.

221
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,159
Then let him have his fill of novelty!

222
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,240
Are you even listening to yourself?

223
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,759
I just don't understand.

224
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:37,639
Why does he get to take my money?

225
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,360
Don't get trapped in your own head.

226
00:12:43,759 --> 00:12:45,279
Step back and look at the big picture.

227
00:12:45,759 --> 00:12:47,000
We give him the money,

228
00:12:47,159 --> 00:12:48,799
like giving a red envelope to a boss.

229
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,640
The boss doesn't need the money,

230
00:12:52,039 --> 00:12:53,960
but they like the
feeling of receiving gifts.

231
00:12:55,799 --> 00:12:58,615
Only by emotionally soothing his
resentment of not getting what he wants

232
00:12:58,639 --> 00:13:00,159
can we truly shake him off.

233
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,080
I don't think so.

234
00:13:03,879 --> 00:13:05,600
What if he keeps pestering you?

235
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:06,840
To deal with people like him,

236
00:13:06,841 --> 00:13:08,038
we have to fight fire with fire.

237
00:13:08,039 --> 00:13:09,279
There's no other way around it.

238
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,799
But we don't have the
power to fight fire with fire.

239
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:13,279
Even if we take him down,

240
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,080
there will be an even greater evil later.

241
00:13:16,039 --> 00:13:17,399
We can only defuse the situation.

242
00:13:18,279 --> 00:13:20,159
Defusing it is our way of survival.

243
00:13:21,559 --> 00:13:22,559
Fine.

244
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,799
Then I think you should just
let him have his fill of novelty.

245
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,158
Once he's had enough,

246
00:13:27,159 --> 00:13:28,799
everything will be defused.

247
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,720
Unlocked successfully.
Please open the door.

248
00:14:17,799 --> 00:14:19,038
I just got back from the temple.

249
00:14:19,039 --> 00:14:20,440
I smell heavily of incense.

250
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,638
I'm going up to the second floor to change.

251
00:14:24,639 --> 00:14:25,639
Make yourself at home.

252
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,976
What would you like to drink?

253
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Do you have coffee?

254
00:14:31,001 --> 00:14:32,359
You asked the right person.

255
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,639
The best Tianyi coffee.

256
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:45,799
Brother Lang.
Yeah?

257
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:49,480
There are some things I want to
ask someone who's been through it.

258
00:14:50,399 --> 00:14:51,399
Troubles?

259
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,360
Unspoken rules.

260
00:14:55,759 --> 00:14:57,559
What makes you so
sure I've been through it?

261
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,440
At least everyone thinks

262
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,678
that someone who hasn't been through it

263
00:15:01,679 --> 00:15:03,679
could never make it in
the entertainment industry.

264
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:05,559
Fair enough.

265
00:15:06,159 --> 00:15:07,399
Tell me about your troubles.

266
00:15:17,759 --> 00:15:19,600
This is your trouble.

267
00:15:21,639 --> 00:15:23,600
This is the solution you chose.

268
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,840
This is Qi Haoyu.

269
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,600
And there are many
others you didn't choose.

270
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,360
If life is a straight line,

271
00:15:34,399 --> 00:15:37,440
connecting it this way or that way

272
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:40,039
will definitely lead to
two different outcomes.

273
00:15:40,879 --> 00:15:42,840
So if we keep making assumptions,

274
00:15:42,879 --> 00:15:44,758
all we can see are

275
00:15:44,759 --> 00:15:46,360
two paths drifting further apart.

276
00:15:52,399 --> 00:15:53,759
Take away the assumptions,

277
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,280
and it goes back to what
Sister Lan always says.

278
00:15:57,399 --> 00:15:58,879
Don't make preconceived notions.

279
00:15:59,399 --> 00:16:01,158
Before the outcome happens,

280
00:16:01,159 --> 00:16:02,479
everything is just an assumption.

281
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,679
What if the outcome is bad?

282
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,999
But right now, you can't
predict the outcome at all.

283
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,360
Will you even think it's
bad once it happens?

284
00:16:13,399 --> 00:16:14,399
That's a bit convoluted.

285
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,759
For example, seven years
ago when I was with Shi Yuhao,

286
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,399
I thought breaking up
would be the worst outcome.

287
00:16:24,799 --> 00:16:26,158
But I never expected
that seven years later,

288
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:28,399
I'd meet someone else, and looking back,

289
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:31,000
what I originally defined
as the worst outcome

290
00:16:31,159 --> 00:16:32,600
actually looks pretty good.

291
00:16:52,519 --> 00:16:54,799
Give the magazine money
to whoever you want.

292
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,720
Thank you.

293
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,519
Director Ou said it very well.

294
00:17:10,759 --> 00:17:12,358
Our movie "Rumination" is

295
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:14,000
a gaze upon life.

296
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:16,039
Let's immerse ourselves together.

297
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:18,896
We're dominating the charts. The
trending topics are all about our company.

298
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,559
How did these few shoot up?

299
00:17:21,799 --> 00:17:24,038
At first, it seemed like they were bought,

300
00:17:24,039 --> 00:17:25,920
but now it's all organic traffic.

301
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,359
Suppress the love story one immediately.
[The "love story" between the two bosses]

302
00:17:28,799 --> 00:17:30,000
Got it, I'll arrange it.

303
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,119
Ms. Fang, another one just shot up.

304
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,518
Jialan's daughter and gene customization.

305
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:42,640
This one is rising fast.

306
00:17:45,359 --> 00:17:47,400
Go prepare the supporting documents first.

307
00:17:47,599 --> 00:17:49,519
Ask Lawyer Shang to draft a legal letter.

308
00:17:50,119 --> 00:17:51,839
Have the PR firm control the comments ASAP.

309
00:17:52,319 --> 00:17:54,359
Ms. Fang, proving our
innocence won't do much good.

310
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,720
I know.

311
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:58,640
The company's artists should
speak up and take a stand now.

312
00:17:59,799 --> 00:18:00,960
What if the ship sinks?

313
00:18:00,990 --> 00:18:04,936
[Many comments all damning the rich and
their choices while lamenting being poor]

314
00:18:29,343 --> 00:18:32,383
[Fans asking what the meaning behind the post is]

315
00:18:32,443 --> 00:18:37,123
["Stop the rumours!" ad nauseum]

316
00:18:38,986 --> 00:18:39,986
Shit.

317
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,599
That's freaking awesome.

318
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:43,160
Hey.

319
00:18:43,161 --> 00:18:45,720
A food blogger uploaded a
dish called "All-Sorts Shrimp."

320
00:18:45,759 --> 00:18:47,599
It's already hit the
top of the trending list.

321
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:51,440
Lang Di, your bait-and-switch
move is brilliant.

322
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,095
Log into my main
account and give it a like.

323
00:18:54,119 --> 00:18:55,119
Sure.

324
00:18:56,736 --> 00:18:59,936
["Upright bodies aren't scared
of tilted shadows" ad nauseum]

325
00:19:05,672 --> 00:19:09,305
Come on, everyone
look at me. Ready, 1, 2, 3.

326
00:19:09,409 --> 00:19:11,183
[The comments repeating a proverb of
essentially "Good people keep good company"]

327
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:15,756
[Comments stating that the genetic modifcation was
a rumor, the company stays on top of the search]

328
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,318
I was organizing my cloud drive today

329
00:19:22,319 --> 00:19:23,639
and stumbled upon this old photo.

330
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,558
Do you guys remember which movie

331
00:19:26,559 --> 00:19:28,440
and which scene this is from?

332
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,920
That summer,

333
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,920
we shot a movie celebrating youth together.

334
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,920
The weather in the south was hot and humid.

335
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,640
As soon as I arrived on set, I
broke out in a full-body rash.

336
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:42,095
After filming wrapped and
we entered post-production,

337
00:19:42,119 --> 00:19:43,999
the producer, Sister
Lan, sent me a screenshot.

338
00:19:44,319 --> 00:19:45,640
Yes, this exact one.

339
00:19:46,119 --> 00:19:48,480
Big and small red rashes all over my body.

340
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,839
Sister Lan said she counted
over a hundred of them.

341
00:19:53,279 --> 00:19:54,479
Sister Lan scolded me back then,

342
00:19:54,503 --> 00:19:56,383
saying I drank eight
cups of iced coffee a day,

343
00:19:56,799 --> 00:19:57,838
chain-smoked,

344
00:19:57,839 --> 00:19:59,200
and didn't take care of my body.

345
00:20:00,119 --> 00:20:02,759
She said my hormones were out of
whack, which caused the breakout.

346
00:20:03,016 --> 00:20:06,119
The footage that needed to be processed
for the whole film was over an hour long.

347
00:20:06,599 --> 00:20:10,319
The post-production budget for
skin-smoothing VFX was going to hit 600,000.

348
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,920
I didn't think much of it at the time.

349
00:20:13,039 --> 00:20:14,920
Then, four months
later, I saw the final cut.

350
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,519
There wasn't a single red rash on my body,

351
00:20:17,839 --> 00:20:19,559
and the footage wasn't overly smoothed out.

352
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,400
Sister Lan said

353
00:20:23,079 --> 00:20:25,599
she and Sister Jialin spent four months

354
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:30,319
smoothing it out frame by
frame. 25 frames per second.

355
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,039
One frame is one picture.

356
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:37,440
An hour of video equals 90,000 pictures.

357
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:41,640
They spent four months
retouching exactly 90,000 pictures.

358
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,000
To ensure there were no skipped frames,

359
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,399
every rash and acne mark had
to be smoothed out in order,

360
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,920
from beginning to end.

361
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:56,720
That's way more than just
90,000 pictures' worth of work.

362
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:01,200
Ms. Fang, Shi Yuhao spoke up for us.

363
00:21:01,839 --> 00:21:03,599
The tide is turning.

364
00:21:05,079 --> 00:21:07,039
They only slept four hours a day,

365
00:21:07,519 --> 00:21:09,095
staring at the screen until
they cried from exhaustion.

366
00:21:09,119 --> 00:21:11,055
Their eyes were searching
for red spots on my body.

367
00:21:11,079 --> 00:21:12,999
Just turning their heads
made their vision blur.

368
00:21:13,799 --> 00:21:16,159
Who with money would willingly
put themselves through that?

369
00:21:19,518 --> 00:21:22,679
Back then, they and we
had absolutely nothing.

370
00:21:59,812 --> 00:22:02,326
["Gods Have Come to Humanity"]

371
00:22:03,796 --> 00:22:06,433
Sister Lan, the novel you
definitely wished for is getting filmed,

372
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:08,123
now even more people
will see your first intention]

373
00:22:08,306 --> 00:22:14,246
[Fans commenting
about the adaptation]

374
00:22:14,359 --> 00:22:16,679
Release the synopsis for Canghuang.

375
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,999
Post the concept posters

376
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,000
and the director's statement.

377
00:22:19,001 --> 00:22:20,559
Release them every hour on the hour.

378
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:26,400
This is more intense
than a war. It's so thrilling!

379
00:22:27,079 --> 00:22:28,720
Canghuang Synopsis.

380
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:31,079
Sister Jialin followed
up with a great move.

381
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:36,919
Canghuang tells the story of the greatest
king in the history of the Qi Kingdom,

382
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:40,159
King Ran Huang, who, to
control human genetic pollution,

383
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:43,798
formed a global army called
the Sea Expeditionary Force.

384
00:22:43,799 --> 00:22:47,839
The Sea God, Bai Jinghua,
served as its first commander.

385
00:22:48,359 --> 00:22:51,758
One man and one god worked together

386
00:22:51,782 --> 00:22:54,982
to create a balanced
world in this Xianxia tale.

387
00:22:55,070 --> 00:22:55,816
[insane gay laugh]

388
00:22:56,220 --> 00:22:58,799
Who would have thought our Xianxia drama

389
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:01,599
would have an anti-gene
customization theme?

390
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:06,039
Sister Lan, you're truly something else.

391
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,359
So ahead of your time.

392
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:10,599
Fourteen years ahead of humanity.

393
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:14,999
Sister Lan.

394
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,640
I miss you so much.

395
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:05,366
[Top search is about the company
mobilizing to make a new fantasy show]

396
00:24:43,153 --> 00:24:44,439
[Han Lu]

397
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:58,920
Lu.

398
00:24:59,119 --> 00:25:00,119
Are you home?

399
00:25:00,319 --> 00:25:01,319
Brother Guo.

400
00:25:07,519 --> 00:25:08,319
Some people

401
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:09,616
are too scared to go home themselves,

402
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:10,720
so they use me as a shield.

403
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,519
Come in, you useless piece of work.

404
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:21,720
Oh, our indispensable
hero returns in triumph!

405
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:27,160
Damn, my pot is growing mold.

406
00:25:30,519 --> 00:25:31,400
You two

407
00:25:31,519 --> 00:25:33,519
are both solving problems in your own ways.

408
00:25:33,559 --> 00:25:35,318
But what matters isn't
whose method is right,

409
00:25:35,319 --> 00:25:37,879
but that you both have the heart
to make things better together.

410
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,719
You have it, and so does he.

411
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,120
So there's nothing wrong with that.

412
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,200
Brother Guo.

413
00:25:44,559 --> 00:25:46,200
You have no idea how he chewed me out.

414
00:25:46,319 --> 00:25:48,159
Brother, this is how I chewed him out.

415
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:48,960
Oh, enough.

416
00:25:48,961 --> 00:25:50,199
Go wash your moldy pot.

417
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:51,200
Fine.

418
00:25:53,799 --> 00:25:56,319
Haoyu bringing up Sister
Lan's early works this time

419
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:58,720
was indeed the most crucial
step in resolving the crisis.

420
00:25:58,839 --> 00:26:01,039
You have to admit his intentions were good.

421
00:26:02,319 --> 00:26:03,599
But his attitude was terrible.

422
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:06,039
Hey, a bad attitude can be corrected.

423
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:08,160
But if the heart is crooked,
there's no saving it.

424
00:26:09,039 --> 00:26:10,319
Who are you calling crooked?

425
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:11,400
Oh, knock it off.

426
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:13,558
A broken pot can't shut a
trashy mouth. Go wash the pot.

427
00:26:13,559 --> 00:26:14,559
Fine.

428
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,959
As for what needed to be said,

429
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:21,559
I think I've already said it all.

430
00:26:22,599 --> 00:26:26,920
You two can settle the rest in bed.

431
00:26:35,079 --> 00:26:36,599
Let me feed you.

432
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,640
Qi Haoyu, back off.

433
00:26:40,839 --> 00:26:41,839
Your mouth is filthy.

434
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:44,440
Filthy or not, you've
kissed it plenty. Come here.

435
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Is it sweet?

436
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,240
Sweet.
Have another bite.

437
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:01,799
Mom, I'm going to become a monk.

438
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,599
Do you remember when you
took me to the temple as a kid?

439
00:27:05,319 --> 00:27:07,240
A master saw me and said,

440
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:09,640
"This child will return sooner or later."

441
00:27:11,599 --> 00:27:13,920
When Jianjun passed
away, Tian was still little.

442
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:16,640
I had to stay in the mortal
world a few more years.

443
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:21,480
Now that I see Lang has
someone to take care of him,

444
00:27:21,839 --> 00:27:23,400
and you have Lang to take care of you,

445
00:27:23,599 --> 00:27:24,920
it's time for me to go back.

446
00:27:26,119 --> 00:27:28,799
I don't want Tian to
be lonely up in heaven.

447
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,640
I'm going to the temple
to chant sutras for him.

448
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:37,400
He likes listening to them.

449
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:38,920
He can hear them.

450
00:27:39,839 --> 00:27:43,400
Since he likes it, I should chant
for him more while I'm still alive.

451
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,079
Go ahead.

452
00:27:51,079 --> 00:27:53,200
Mom is still going strong.

453
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:55,119
I don't need you.

454
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:08,720
It's truly a tragedy for a
parent to bury their child.

455
00:28:39,636 --> 00:28:41,416
[Changyang At Home]

456
00:28:41,956 --> 00:28:43,503
[Mom has decided to become a nun]

457
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,480
Is it him?

458
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:19,799
I can't see clearly.

459
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,520
It's definitely him, no mistake about it.

460
00:29:22,839 --> 00:29:23,879
Auntie, let me tell you.

461
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:25,879
I've compared it with
your photo so many times.

462
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:26,960
They look exactly the same.

463
00:29:27,839 --> 00:29:28,640
Auntie.

464
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:30,880
We can't let my brother die in vain.

465
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,279
Hey, listen to me.

466
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:33,798
I've looked into this movie.

467
00:29:33,799 --> 00:29:35,319
That little boy is the lead actor.

468
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:38,639
And the director won some kind of award.

469
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,616
Anyway, this movie got a lot of
traffic as soon as it was released.

470
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:42,440
Do you know what traffic means?

471
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:45,880
Traffic means money, Auntie.

472
00:29:46,279 --> 00:29:47,119
Hey, let me tell you.

473
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:49,440
You and Uncle don't need
to worry about a thing.

474
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,640
Leave everything to me.

475
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:52,440
What do you need to do?

476
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:56,880
Sit back, talk, and collect the money.

477
00:29:58,279 --> 00:30:01,200
Before my son got into the car accident,

478
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:03,519
he came back and told us

479
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:07,319
that he liked men.

480
00:30:10,319 --> 00:30:11,640
It was this person.

481
00:30:12,119 --> 00:30:13,720
He looks neither like a man nor a woman.

482
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:16,079
He seduced my son.

483
00:30:22,839 --> 00:30:24,880
I'll write a script for you tomorrow.

484
00:30:29,999 --> 00:30:31,518
Director Li, you flatter me too much.

485
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,679
But I really can't give
you an answer right now.

486
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:35,000
I'm also still waiting for news.

487
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:38,480
Do you have other acting offers?

488
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:40,039
No.

489
00:30:42,839 --> 00:30:44,639
My friend led a team
into the primeval forest.

490
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,440
There's no signal right now.
I can't reach him either.

491
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:47,440
I have to wait until he comes out

492
00:30:47,441 --> 00:30:49,681
and discuss it with him
before I can give you an answer.

493
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:51,680
A very important friend?

494
00:30:53,039 --> 00:30:54,039
Yes.

495
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:57,480
Director Li, rest assured.

496
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:59,295
If I take on any roles in
the second half of the year,

497
00:30:59,319 --> 00:31:00,440
it will definitely be yours.

498
00:31:00,599 --> 00:31:01,599
Old man.

499
00:31:01,720 --> 00:31:02,999
The director from my last show

500
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,078
has already deleted that intimate scene.

501
00:31:04,372 --> 00:31:05,599
It's already been filmed.

502
00:31:05,799 --> 00:31:07,038
I badgered him for days

503
00:31:07,039 --> 00:31:08,000
before the director finally agreed.
It was just shot with camera tricks.

504
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:09,920
Shot with camera tricks?

505
00:31:10,039 --> 00:31:11,240
It must look awful.

506
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:13,279
Did you really need to badger him?

507
00:31:13,799 --> 00:31:15,519
You're so full of hot air.

508
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,599
Not a single word of truth. I'm hanging up.

509
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,160
Sister Jialin.

510
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:20,240
You're back.

511
00:31:20,799 --> 00:31:23,160
Yeah. Don't tell Qinglang I'm back.

512
00:31:30,799 --> 00:31:32,919
There's absolutely nothing
wrong with this car. Look.

513
00:31:37,759 --> 00:31:39,039
Earth Pay OK?

514
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,160
Okay.

515
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:47,640
Auntie, I'll have this apple here.

516
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:54,400
Auntie.

517
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:03,000
I've paid, Auntie.

518
00:32:13,300 --> 00:32:15,846
[Haiyuan Hostel]

519
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:31,639
Season 2 of "Still a
Teenager Upon Return" is

520
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:33,960
title-sponsored by the Hot Love brand.

521
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:35,240
Entering Xizhou.

522
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,920
Still a Teenager Upon Return.

523
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:38,136
With the wind and moon as witnesses,

524
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:40,280
wishing you peace deep in
your bones year after year.

525
00:32:41,079 --> 00:32:42,735
We're discussing an
endorsement next Tuesday.

526
00:32:42,759 --> 00:32:43,798
I'll send you the location.

527
00:32:43,799 --> 00:32:44,960
Drive yourself over.

528
00:32:45,053 --> 00:32:46,473
[On a call with Vicky the Agent]

529
00:32:53,880 --> 00:32:55,696
The variety show with
you two is really popular.

530
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:58,240
A few new endorsement offers
came in. Do you want to take them?

531
00:32:58,279 --> 00:32:59,079
You arrange it.

532
00:32:59,080 --> 00:33:00,160
No joint endorsements.

533
00:33:11,900 --> 00:33:14,899
(Changyang at Home)

534
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:18,500
(Someone in June, is
the assessment over? ~)

535
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:30,199
When you need me the most,

536
00:33:30,200 --> 00:33:31,499
I can't be by your side,

537
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:33,599
nor can I message you in real-time.

538
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:36,299
But I'll write messages in
advance and schedule them for you.

539
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:38,399
I promise you'll receive a
message from me every day.

540
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:40,360
We'll never lose touch
for the rest of our lives.

541
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:45,000
(Feng Qinglang: Can you really
do it just because you promise?)

542
00:33:48,500 --> 00:33:51,300
I bet when you saw yesterday's
message, you definitely said,

543
00:33:51,700 --> 00:33:53,620
"Can you really do it just
because you promise?"

544
00:33:53,700 --> 00:33:56,299
Maybe due to outside
interference, I might not be able to.

545
00:33:56,300 --> 00:33:57,999
But when I made the promise,

546
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:00,400
my heart was bound to making it happen.

547
00:34:00,500 --> 00:34:04,300
(You're bound to making it happen,
so do you want to seperate from me?)

548
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:12,119
Let me guess

549
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:14,679
what you'll say when you
see yesterday's message.

550
00:34:15,079 --> 00:34:16,280
You've read too many scripts.

551
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:19,336
Someone who loves to nitpick words
will definitely make a fuss about "bound."

552
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:22,480
A petty person would get jealous of
me being bound to something else.

553
00:34:23,119 --> 00:34:26,239
I know, I need to correct my
last sentence from yesterday.

554
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:29,239
My heart can only ever be bound to you.

555
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:31,360
While I'm at it, let me predict

556
00:34:31,480 --> 00:34:32,960
what you'll say today.

557
00:34:33,079 --> 00:34:34,719
"Am I petty?"

558
00:34:36,680 --> 00:34:39,279
You guessed wrong. Today I want to say,

559
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:40,960
I miss you so much.
